    "q-32277": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32277",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Calculate the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ with respect to $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
