    "q-32278": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32278",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find the second derivative of $f(t)=2{t}^{3}\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2})\\,j+(5{t}^{3}+\\sqrt{5}t-2\\sqrt{5})\\,k$ with respect to $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}+\\sqrt{5}t-2\\sqrt{5})\\,k \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\,i-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2t)\\,j+(15{t}^{2}+\\sqrt{5})\\,k \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2t)\\,j+(15{t}^{2}+\\sqrt{5})\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}+\\sqrt{5})\\,k \\\\  & =12t\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2)\\,j+30t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
